1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,633
<i>Liza was supposed to surrender.</i>

2
00:00:01,767 --> 00:00:03,233
<i>Something bad must have
happened to her.</i>

3
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:04,667
<i> I know where she might be.</i>

4
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:05,900
<i> That's the only place I know.</i>

5
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:07,533
<i> They don't trust me that much.</i>

6
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:09,767
<i>I've been through
a lot with this person.</i>

7
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,500
<i>I want to be the one
to catch him myself.</i>

8
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:12,733
<i>Where will you hold the meeting?</i>

9
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:13,867
<i> I have a plan.</i>

10
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,200
<i> Are you attending tomorrow?</i>

11
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,033
<i> Yes, where will this be held?</i>

12
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,367
<i> At the old quarry.</i>

13
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,467
<i> Is Jin Ho still asleep?</i>

14
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:20,733
<i> Did Oppa escape again?</i>

15
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:22,233
<i> I think he's looking for Liza.</i>

16
00:00:22,367 --> 00:00:23,567
<i> The Korean escaped from me.</i>

17
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,633
<i> He even took my gun.</i>

18
00:00:24,767 --> 00:00:26,000
<i> I'm coming for you, Liza.</i>

19
00:00:26,133 --> 00:00:27,133
<i> Don't worry, Liza.</i>

20
00:00:27,267 --> 00:00:28,900
<i>I won't prolong your suffering.</i>

21
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:30,067
<i> Follow that car.</i>

22
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,733
<i> Where are we taking Liza?</i>

23
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:33,767
<i>Anywhere we pass
where there are no people.</i>

24
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:35,167
<i> Let's find Jin Ho!</i>

25
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:36,967
<i>We're following
a subject right now.</i>

26
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,833
<i>- Possible target.
- That's Dad.</i>

27
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:39,700
<i> Block them!</i>

28
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:41,633
<i> Who are they following?</i>

29
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:45,633
<i> [OBB]</i>

30
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:00,533
- Bolagos Police!
- What is it, Sir?

31
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:02,633
- Who are you with?
- I'm alone, Sir.

32
00:01:02,767 --> 00:01:03,800
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

33
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:05,500
Window.

34
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:07,567
There it is.

35
00:01:10,867 --> 00:01:14,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

36
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:19,467
Sorry, we're just looking
for someone.

37
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,967
It's okay, Sir.

38
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:25,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

39
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:33,500
Where are you, Berdugo?

40
00:01:33,633 --> 00:01:37,667
[REVVING]

41
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:49,800
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

42
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:53,267
That's beautiful, Berdugo.

43
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:56,133
It's worth every peso
I spent on it.

44
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:58,233
I'll christen this now.

45
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:02,133
Stop the car.

46
00:02:08,367 --> 00:02:10,400
Go on, let Liza out.

47
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:12,233
Go on, let her out.
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:02:12,367 --> 00:02:14,033
Make sure no one sees you.

49
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:15,400
Okay, Boss.

50
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:19,633
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

51
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:37,300
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,867
[MUFFLED PLEADING]

53
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:55,533
[MUFFLED PLEADING]

54
00:02:55,667 --> 00:02:56,600
Goodbye, Liza.

55
00:02:56,733 --> 00:02:57,667
[MUFFLED PLEADING]

56
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,300
[GUN FIRES]

57
00:02:59,433 --> 00:03:04,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:03:08,867 --> 00:03:10,167
That's for you.

59
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:13,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

60
00:03:14,767 --> 00:03:16,700
Are you sure, Berdugo?

61
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,867
You are the only one loyal
to me and our group.

62
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,467
That's your reward.

63
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,700
Thank you.

64
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:26,800
Everything you ask me to do,
I'll do.

65
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,500
I know.

66
00:03:29,633 --> 00:03:33,733
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

67
00:03:37,633 --> 00:03:39,367
What's that on the side
of the road?

68
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:41,300
Stop the car.

69
00:03:41,433 --> 00:03:45,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

70
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:53,933
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

71
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,600
It's Liza!

72
00:03:56,267 --> 00:03:58,633
X-Alpha unit, come in.

73
00:03:58,767 --> 00:04:00,100
<i> Yes, Cruz?</i>

74
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:01,700
Major, positive.

75
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:03,933
We found Liza here.

76
00:04:04,067 --> 00:04:04,867
She was salvaged.

77
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,833
It was done in the grassland.

78
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:08,567
<i> Okay, we're on our way!</i>

79
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:11,667
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

80
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,167
Liza!

81
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:15,333
Liza, Liza...

82
00:04:15,467 --> 00:04:16,700
Liza...

83
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:19,267
Sir, let's take her
to the hospital!

84
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:20,833
No.

85
00:04:22,433 --> 00:04:23,967
Please tell Jin Ho...

86
00:04:24,967 --> 00:04:26,833
I'm sorry.

87
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,200
No, you'll tell him yourself.

88
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:29,700
We'll take you to the hospital.

89
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:31,467
Liza, where are your companions?

90
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,233
Where is Berdugo?

91
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,167
Quarry.

92
00:04:41,433 --> 00:04:43,000
Quarry?

93
00:04:43,133 --> 00:04:47,367
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:04:56,200 --> 00:05:00,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:05:00,167 --> 00:05:01,767
Thank you.

96
00:05:01,933 --> 00:05:05,933
[CROWD APPLAUDING]

97
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:08,333
Thank you!

98
00:05:08,467 --> 00:05:10,700
Thank you! Thank you, everyone!

99
00:05:10,833 --> 00:05:12,000
Thank you! You're all...

100
00:05:12,133 --> 00:05:13,600
You're all too kind.

101
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:15,067
Right, Hon?

102
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:18,667
They're not only kind
but, also very generous.

103
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,867
That's true.

104
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,933
You know, with all your help,

105
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:23,700
the Hope Circle Foundation

106
00:05:23,833 --> 00:05:27,933
will be able to build
the Angel Sanctuary.

107
00:05:28,067 --> 00:05:29,633
And we're doing all this

108
00:05:29,767 --> 00:05:33,700
for the children, our future.

109
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:37,833
So, on behalf of the whole
foundation and the children,

110
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,700
we would like to thank
all of you so much.

111
00:05:40,833 --> 00:05:42,000
Thank you.

112
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:43,067
[CROWD APPLAUDING]

113
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,500
Thank you.

114
00:05:44,633 --> 00:05:46,333
Thank you so much.

115
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:48,767
Thank you so much.

116
00:05:49,867 --> 00:05:51,867
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

117
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,867
<i> Picture, picture!</i>

118
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:56,167
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

119
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:01,733
[AMBULANCE SIREN WAILING]

120
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:03,833
Looks like they're eliminating
each other.

121
00:06:04,967 --> 00:06:06,633
Maybe they're just eliminating

122
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:09,100
those who turned against them.

123
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:11,800
Because isn't that what they
wanted to do to Jin Ho?

124
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:15,800
Dad, do you have any news about
Jin Ho's whereabouts?

125
00:06:15,933 --> 00:06:18,100
Maybe he already left
the country.

126
00:06:18,233 --> 00:06:22,833
What's important is that I get
to the quarry Liza mentioned.

127
00:06:22,967 --> 00:06:24,367
Maybe Berdugo is there.

128
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,633
We'll come with you, Major.

129
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:26,767
No.

130
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:28,500
Just go home.

131
00:06:28,633 --> 00:06:30,667
There are guards there too.

132
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,233
Can I count on you?

133
00:06:33,533 --> 00:06:34,500
Cruz...

134
00:06:34,633 --> 00:06:37,000
give them their phones.

135
00:06:37,133 --> 00:06:40,067
If there's a problem,
just call me.

136
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:43,433
I have a strong feeling
Jin Ho won't leave the country.

137
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:45,867
Where could our friend be now?

138
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Go ahead, you can leave now.

139
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:51,100
Take care, Dad.

140
00:06:51,233 --> 00:06:53,133
You take care too.

141
00:06:53,267 --> 00:06:57,267
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

142
00:07:02,367 --> 00:07:05,500
Cruz, this day won't end

143
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:08,000
without us getting Berdugo.

144
00:07:08,133 --> 00:07:12,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:28,033
[REVVING]

146
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:31,100
[HEAVY MUSIC PLAYING]

147
00:07:31,233 --> 00:07:32,900
<i> I'm sorry, Liza.</i>

148
00:07:34,933 --> 00:07:37,833
[REVVING]

149
00:07:37,967 --> 00:07:39,233
[GUN FIRES]

150
00:07:39,367 --> 00:07:43,367
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

151
00:07:46,733 --> 00:07:50,367
[REVVING]

152
00:07:50,533 --> 00:07:55,167
[HEAVY MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:10,833
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

154
00:08:10,967 --> 00:08:12,433
<i> Liza...</i>

155
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,567
<i> Look at me, Liza.</i>

156
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:17,633
<i> No...</i>

157
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:19,767
<i> no, Liza!</i>

158
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,367
<i> No...</i>

159
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:25,200
[SHOUTS]

160
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:29,100
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

161
00:08:42,433 --> 00:08:45,767
[POLICE SIREN WAILING
IN DISTANCE]

162
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:49,900
[MOTORCYCLE REVVING]

163
00:08:52,233 --> 00:08:55,033
Sir, here's the CCTV footage.

164
00:09:02,533 --> 00:09:05,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

165
00:09:05,667 --> 00:09:07,867
- Impressive, huh.
- What kind of gun is that?

166
00:09:09,633 --> 00:09:11,800
These syndicates
are something else.

167
00:09:12,367 --> 00:09:14,000
Even their guns are customized.

168
00:09:14,133 --> 00:09:16,400
Who could be handling
those guns?

169
00:09:16,533 --> 00:09:18,433
Only one person comes to mind.

170
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:22,000
Send a copy of that to
the Chief.

171
00:09:22,133 --> 00:09:25,267
Also find out who the vehicle
is registered to,

172
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,800
and call for additional backup.

173
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,967
Captain, thank you very much.

174
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:31,900
All right, Sir.

175
00:09:32,033 --> 00:09:33,267
We'll go ahead.

176
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:36,200
Men, let's move!

177
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:41,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:48,333 --> 00:09:52,233
[REVVING]

179
00:09:59,967 --> 00:10:01,067
Andrew, where are you going?

180
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:03,900
Major said we should stay at the
house for the meantime.

181
00:10:04,067 --> 00:10:06,067
Andrew, stay here, please.

182
00:10:08,067 --> 00:10:09,333
Okay.

183
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:12,333
- [PHONE RINGING]
- Oh, answer it.

184
00:10:12,467 --> 00:10:14,067
Put it on speaker, speaker.

185
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,133
Hello?

186
00:10:17,267 --> 00:10:18,500
Hello, Joey?

187
00:10:18,633 --> 00:10:20,100
Hey, Oppa, why did you
escape again?

188
00:10:20,233 --> 00:10:21,800
You just created trouble.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:24,533
Jin Ho, where are you?

190
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:25,667
Oh, wait a minute.

191
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:27,767
You're asking him
too many questions right away.

192
00:10:28,633 --> 00:10:30,667
Jin Ho, we're worried about you.

193
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,533
<i> We're at our house now.</i>

194
00:10:32,667 --> 00:10:33,967
Just come here.

195
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:35,533
I know.

196
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:38,233
And I'm sorry to leave you all
like this.

197
00:10:38,367 --> 00:10:40,100
Jin Ho, listen to me.

198
00:10:40,233 --> 00:10:41,733
<i>Jin Ho, you're smart enough
to understand</i>

199
00:10:41,867 --> 00:10:43,867
<i>that you're only making
your situation worse.</i>

200
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,033
<i> Come here.</i>

201
00:10:45,167 --> 00:10:48,367
<i>We, your friends,
can still help you fix this.</i>

202
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,000
Okay?

203
00:10:52,267 --> 00:10:53,533
Please, Jin Ho.

204
00:10:54,267 --> 00:10:57,500
I am so thankful to all of you,
for being my friends.

205
00:10:57,633 --> 00:10:58,933
<i> Especially you, Joey.</i>

206
00:10:59,067 --> 00:11:01,567
<i>But I can't go there right now.</i>

207
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:04,800
Because I have to avenge Liza.

208
00:11:04,933 --> 00:11:14,900
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

209
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:26,400
[GUN COCKS]

210
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:30,933
You will have your revenge,
Liza.

211
00:11:31,067 --> 00:11:36,200
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:11:37,567 --> 00:11:39,833
Sometimes, I get annoyed
at Jin Ho too.

213
00:11:39,967 --> 00:11:41,533
But like you said,

214
00:11:42,533 --> 00:11:43,633
he is our friend.

215
00:11:43,767 --> 00:11:45,133
Let's go, let's find him.

216
00:11:51,433 --> 00:11:53,500
Congrats to all of us.

217
00:11:53,633 --> 00:11:55,800
Ah, I'm so excited, really.

218
00:11:56,733 --> 00:11:58,767
You're so lucky, Mr. Limjoco.

219
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:01,467
Your wife is really so kind.

220
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,500
I know. I married a saint.
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:12:03,633 --> 00:12:07,633
That's why I hope she'll be the
key for me to enter heaven.

222
00:12:07,767 --> 00:12:08,533
Wow.

223
00:12:08,667 --> 00:12:09,667
Oh, my husband,

224
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:13,233
he way he talks,
it's as if he's a bad person.

225
00:12:13,367 --> 00:12:14,933
You really are something else.

226
00:12:15,100 --> 00:12:16,633
[PHONE CHIMES]

227
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:22,067
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

228
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:27,767
- Hon, excuse me.
- Yes?

229
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:28,900
I just need to check something.

230
00:12:29,033 --> 00:12:30,200
Ah, okay.

231
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:31,800
Excuse.

232
00:12:31,933 --> 00:12:36,267
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:13:02,567 --> 00:13:06,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

234
00:13:12,967 --> 00:13:14,967
I got you, Berdugo.

235
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:17,967
Are you sure you want to do
this, Jin Ho?

236
00:13:18,733 --> 00:13:20,867
You're making a big mistake.

237
00:13:28,367 --> 00:13:32,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:13:36,367 --> 00:13:39,667
You must have heard the news
of your beloved Liza.

239
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:42,233
I saw you with my own eyes.

240
00:13:43,433 --> 00:13:45,200
You killed her.

241
00:13:45,333 --> 00:13:46,967
And now...

242
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:49,267
it is your time to die!

243
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:12,233
What's the meaning of this?

244
00:14:12,767 --> 00:14:15,667
Aren't you Major Delgado,
the husband of Clarissa?

245
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,400
Someone told us

246
00:14:17,533 --> 00:14:20,033
that the group
we're looking for is here

247
00:14:20,167 --> 00:14:21,933
along with their leader.

248
00:14:22,067 --> 00:14:22,800
What?

249
00:14:23,733 --> 00:14:26,867
These are decent
and kind people here.

250
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,333
They are the sponsors
of my foundation.

251
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:32,100
Ma'am, we're sorry.

252
00:14:32,233 --> 00:14:34,000
We're just doing our job.

253
00:14:34,133 --> 00:14:37,067
And besides, it's hard
to trust so easily.

254
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:39,633
Fine.

255
00:14:40,267 --> 00:14:41,167
Search the area!

256
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:42,667
Yes, Sir!

257
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:47,000
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

258
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:52,633
This is for Liza.

259
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,000
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:14:54,133 --> 00:14:57,933
Then do it or else...

261
00:14:58,067 --> 00:15:00,667
I'm going to kill you next!

262
00:15:06,233 --> 00:15:08,200
[GUN FIRING]

263
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:09,500
- [CROWD CLAMORING]
- Sir...

264
00:15:09,633 --> 00:15:10,900
[GUN FIRING]
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:15:11,033 --> 00:15:12,267
It sounded like the shots
came from there!

266
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:14,833
Let's track it!
You stay here!

267
00:15:14,967 --> 00:15:17,033
[GUN FIRING]

268
00:15:17,733 --> 00:15:21,333
[GUN FIRING]

269
00:15:22,667 --> 00:15:26,800
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

270
00:15:26,933 --> 00:15:29,433
[GUN FIRING]

271
00:15:29,567 --> 00:15:30,733
[GROANS]

272
00:15:30,867 --> 00:15:33,633
[GUN FIRING]

273
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:38,300
[GUN FIRING]

274
00:15:38,433 --> 00:15:42,433
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

275
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:51,200
Jin Ho!

276
00:15:51,333 --> 00:15:54,533
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

277
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,933
Jin Ho!

278
00:16:01,833 --> 00:16:03,233
Berdugo!

279
00:16:03,533 --> 00:16:04,700
Good thing I found you!

280
00:16:04,833 --> 00:16:06,333
We need to leave!

281
00:16:06,467 --> 00:16:07,867
Mr. Stuart didn't come!

282
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,633
You scared me!

283
00:16:10,567 --> 00:16:12,233
Where's Berdugo?

284
00:16:12,733 --> 00:16:14,767
But Joey, we need to leave now.

285
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:16,967
Where's Berdugo?

286
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:19,867
Berdugo?
He's here?

287
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:20,800
Yes.

288
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:21,867
Where?

289
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,433
Let's go!

290
00:16:25,867 --> 00:16:26,867
Berdugo!

291
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,267
[GUN FIRING]

292
00:16:32,733 --> 00:16:33,833
We need to get him out of here

293
00:16:33,967 --> 00:16:36,167
before Berdugo finishes him!

294
00:16:36,667 --> 00:16:37,700
- Come on! Let's go, let's go!
- Let's go!

295
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:38,933
How about Berdugo?

296
00:16:39,067 --> 00:16:40,500
- Let's go!
- He killed Liza!

297
00:16:40,633 --> 00:16:42,867
Dad will deal with him!
Let's go!

298
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:48,433
[GUN FIRING]

299
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:52,700
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

300
00:16:52,833 --> 00:16:54,367
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

301
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:58,467
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

302
00:17:10,967 --> 00:17:14,367
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

303
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,367
Berdugo, surrender now!

304
00:17:16,533 --> 00:17:17,033
[GUN FIRING]

305
00:17:17,167 --> 00:17:18,567
Berdugo!

306
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:21,367
[GUN FIRING]

307
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,967
[GUN FIRING]

308
00:17:27,267 --> 00:17:29,100
I'm out of bullets, Berdugo.

309
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,767
I'll give you ten seconds!

310
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,567
You still have a chance to live!

311
00:17:36,233 --> 00:17:40,367
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:17:52,167 --> 00:17:56,200
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:00,633
We have no choice.

314
00:18:04,733 --> 00:18:07,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

315
00:18:08,367 --> 00:18:09,233
<i> Any moment now...</i>

316
00:18:09,367 --> 00:18:11,633
Finally, you can live
peacefully now.

317
00:18:12,433 --> 00:18:13,467
That's right.

318
00:18:13,600 --> 00:18:15,633
Now, Mom and I can truly say

319
00:18:15,767 --> 00:18:18,000
our lives are back to normal.

320
00:18:18,133 --> 00:18:20,200
We no longer need to watch
our back, Mom,

321
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:22,500
afraid that someone

322
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:24,233
has bad intentions toward us,
right?

323
00:18:24,367 --> 00:18:25,733
That's right.

324
00:18:25,867 --> 00:18:28,700
And at last,
we can breathe freely.

325
00:18:28,833 --> 00:18:30,633
Thank God.

326
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:34,067
Good morning, everybody.

327
00:18:36,233 --> 00:18:38,267
At long last, we got him.

328
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,000
<i>Berdugo has finally been caught.
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

329
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,733
Oh, there's Miguel.

330
00:18:41,867 --> 00:18:43,567
Your father!

331
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,733
<i> Thanks to the tireless efforts</i>

332
00:18:45,867 --> 00:18:47,600
<i> of our police</i>

333
00:18:47,733 --> 00:18:50,967
<i> led by Major Miguel Delgado.</i>

334
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:55,300
[CROWD APPLAUDING]

335
00:18:57,533 --> 00:19:00,500
- [WHOOPING]
- That's my father!

336
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,900
Turn on the TV.

337
00:19:03,033 --> 00:19:07,033
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

338
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:09,867
Okay.

339
00:19:10,300 --> 00:19:11,200
Thank you.

340
00:19:11,333 --> 00:19:12,933
<i>Even the Department
of Drug Enforcement</i>

341
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:15,967
<i>was part of the search
for Berdugo</i>

342
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:17,667
<i> And today...</i>

343
00:19:18,267 --> 00:19:20,867
<i> he was captured.</i>

344
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,367
Now...

345
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:26,033
let's allow Major Delgado
to tell us

346
00:19:26,167 --> 00:19:28,500
how Berdugo was caught.

347
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:31,033
<i> Major Delgado.</i>

348
00:19:31,533 --> 00:19:35,467
[CROWD APPLAUDING]

349
00:19:36,867 --> 00:19:38,500
Good day.

350
00:19:39,633 --> 00:19:42,233
It was difficult, exhausting,

351
00:19:42,367 --> 00:19:44,200
and I even had to risk my life

352
00:19:44,333 --> 00:19:45,900
to capture Berdugo.

353
00:19:46,033 --> 00:19:47,667
But even though he was slick,

354
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:51,767
we tracked him down at a quarry

355
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:54,500
with his associates.

356
00:19:54,633 --> 00:19:56,333
<i> Berdugo's group</i>

357
00:19:56,467 --> 00:20:01,367
<i>is the biggest drug dealer
in the Visayas.</i>

358
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,600
So where is Berdugo now?

359
00:20:03,767 --> 00:20:04,833
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:20:04,967 --> 00:20:06,167
He's right there.

361
00:20:07,733 --> 00:20:11,000
Now, we will see the face...

362
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:13,967
behind the name Berdugo.

363
00:20:15,967 --> 00:20:17,400
Cruz.

364
00:20:17,533 --> 00:20:21,500
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

365
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:27,400
So that's Berdugo.

366
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:30,733
<i> That man right there.</i>

367
00:20:31,133 --> 00:20:35,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

368
00:20:44,367 --> 00:20:48,500
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:20:51,900 --> 00:20:53,767
I want to get my revenge.

370
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:56,033
He may not be dead,
but he's been caught.

371
00:20:56,167 --> 00:20:57,400
This is the one
I fought with before,

372
00:20:57,533 --> 00:20:59,367
and Tomas knows him too.

373
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:02,367
To be honest, my business with
Matias is fine

374
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:04,133
since his food business
is thriving.

375
00:21:04,267 --> 00:21:05,200
But you told me before

376
00:21:05,333 --> 00:21:06,833
your business was textiles.

377
00:21:06,967 --> 00:21:08,733
It feels like
I found him too easily.

378
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,900
I have a hunch,
which I can't explain.

379
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:13,600
Nice to meet the daughter
of the bravest man I know.

380
00:21:13,733 --> 00:21:15,433
I think I've heard
his voice before.

381
00:21:15,567 --> 00:21:18,133
I'm right in front of you,
and you still can't do anything.

382
00:21:18,267 --> 00:21:19,933
Do you think I'd stop?

383
00:21:20,067 --> 00:21:21,667
Follow your gut, my son.

384
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:24,200
Everything is not
what it seems to be.

385
00:21:24,333 --> 00:21:25,300
What do you mean?
